Colormap remap-LUT corruption FUN_0000_9e60 / FUN_0000_ac70 (extender op-0x18 MAP-LOAD, the
C32.KLC colormap DATA gate to first in-mission terrain pixels).  ROOT CAUSE (runtime-proven with
stage-by-stage buffer dumps + asm-verified vs re_out/fist_image.bin):

  The C32.KLC colormap DECODES CORRECTLY -- FUN_0000_643c fills the 512x512 buffer at DAT_85b8 with
  262144 real texels / 248 distinct palette indices.  The corruption is the palette-reduction REMAP
  pass FUN_0000_9ec0 -> FUN_0000_9e60, which rebuilds every texel through a 256-entry remap LUT
  (DAT_85c0).  9e60 fills the LUT: for each source palette entry it sets ac68/69/6a = the entry's RGB,
  calls the nearest-colour search FUN_0000_ac70, and stores the result (asm 9ea5 `mov [edi],bl`).

  Two interlocking dropped-register bugs collapsed the LUT to the single constant 0x04:
   (1) FUN_0000_ac70 leaves the nearest reduced-palette index in EBX/BL (asm acdc `mov ebx,ebp`,
       ebp = the palette index walked in lockstep with esi), but the pristine decompile (and patch
       207, which fixed only the distance tables) tracked ONLY the best DISTANCE (edx/uVar5) and
       DROPPED both the ebp index counter and the `mov ebx,ebp` return.
   (2) With ac70 returning nothing, 9e60's `mov [edi],bl` had no source -- Ghidra substituted the
       phantom param_1 (= AL live-in = the constant 4 that 9ec0 passes), so EVERY LUT entry = 4.

  Post-9ec0 the whole 512x512 colormap became 0x04, then bdc4 upsampled it to a uniform 2048x2048
  0x04 plane -> the located voxel render (93c0) drew ONE colour.

FIX (asm-verified, 0xac70..0xace5 + 0x9e60):
   - ac70: restore the ebp index counter (start = DAT_ac64, +1 per iter) and the ebx best-index
     capture on each improvement (`edx=edi; ebx=ebp; if(edi==0) return`), and RETURN ebx.  Return
     type void -> undefined4.
   - 9e60: store the low byte of ac70's return (`*param_3 = (undefined1)FUN_0000_ac70();`) instead of
     the phantom param_1.

Class: dropped multi-register return (extraout / __allregs) + phantom-arg substitution -- the docs'
taxonomy.  Cascade-only (9e60/ac70/9ec0 reached ONLY via the op-0x18 mission map-load palette
reduction; the 19 menu/dialog verify flows never load a mission map) => behaviour-neutral: verify
19/19, default boot unchanged, mainmenu 3a6ff1c5.  Verified live: post-9ec0 the colormap holds the
real remapped terrain indices (multi-colour), not a uniform 0x04.
